Finally, since by assumption $u \in C^3(\Omega)$, $\[(\cof  D^2 u)\]=0$. In addition, by definition $\{\!\{\cof D^2 v \}\!\}$ is continuous and $Du$ is continuous by the assumption on $u$. Thus $\[\{\!\{\cof D^2 v \}\!\} D u \]=0$ on each interior edge. The statement about $A'(u;v,\phi)$ easily follows.
